   "source": [
    "# Twin4Build: Building Space with Space Heater Example\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to create and simulate a building space model with a space heater using Twin4Build. You'll learn how to:\n",
    "1. Create a building space with thermal parameters\n",
    "2. Set up a space heater with optimization capabilities\n",
    "3. Configure various schedules (occupancy, temperature, solar radiation)\n",
    "4. Connect components and create a complete building model\n",
    "5. Optimize the space heater operation to maintain comfort while minimizing energy use\n",
    "\n",
    "This example is particularly useful for understanding:\n",
    "- How to model and control heating systems\n",
    "- Thermal mass and insulation effects\n",
    "- Occupancy patterns and comfort requirements\n",
    "- Solar radiation impact\n",
    "- Optimization of building control strategies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup\n",
    "First, let's install and import the necessary packages. If you're running this in Google Colab, uncomment the pip install line.\n",
    "Note that colab has a dependency issue and asks you to restart the runtime. It will work after you restart the runtime and run the cell a 2nd time.  "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# %pip install twin4build # Uncomment in google colab\n",
    "import twin4build as tb\n",
    "import datetime\n",
    "from dateutil import tz\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Create the Model\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's create a new model instance. This will be our container for all the building components."
